From: SheepyLord <37598021+SheepyLord@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 04:16:01 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] Atmosphere: cloud genera per weather, a sun disc and a high
 cloud layer

Numos's clouds were one layer for every weather, too thin to shade, and an
overcast sky kept km-wide gaps; the sun was only the sky's Mie glow.

- Weather fields for the cloud genera: the low layer's base, edge billows,
  cell size and bake cover (nvdfNominalCoverage, a step: one re-bake per
  change of weather, and above 1 a closed deck), the middle deck
  (altocumulus, altostratus) and a high layer (cirrus cover, the shares of
  cirrus, cirrostratus and cirrocumulus, optical depth). The twelve presets
  map to genera, with densities of 3.5-8 so the clouds shade.
- The sun disc for primary rays: sunSize across, limb-darkened, coloured by
  the air, its centre held to 48 times the daylight, behind the clouds by
  their transmittance to the fourth power; hands over to the eclipse disc.
  rtx.atmosphere.sunDiskEnable, sunDiskBrightness, sunDiskLimbDarkening.
- A 2D high cloud layer at cirrusAltitude: fibrous streaks along the wind,
  an even veil with the 22 degree halo, grains in rows; ice scattering, lit
  by the sun from its own height, the sky, the ground and the moon; it dims
  only the skylight made above it. Detail fades with the pixel footprint;
  other rays take a coarse version. rtx.atmosphere.cirrus*.
- The middle deck skips its march at zero cover; the galaxy band and the
  nebula of the night-sky image wait for astronomical twilight.
- The dev menu: Sun Disc, High Clouds, Edge Billows; weather-owned values
  shown greyed. Catalogs regenerated and translated; RtxOptions.md.
